  "description": "BEMBEE crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C87 H75 Lu4 N3 O17,C7 H8,2(C5 H5 N1). From the CIF bond table, Lu1 (Lu) has 6 O neighbors; Lu2 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu3 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu4 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.416-3.685 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.37-111.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C87H75N3O17Lu4.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
